+.TH EDUKA-ORCA 1 "September 2026" "Eduka-Orca 50.3" "Edukasaun OS"
+.SH NAME
+eduka-orca, eduka-orca-toggle, eduka-orca-autostart \- Orca screen reader for Eduka-Desktop
+.SH SYNOPSIS
+.B eduka-orca
+.RI [ orca-options ]
+.br
+.B eduka-orca-toggle
+.br
+.B eduka-orca-autostart
+.SH DESCRIPTION
+Eduka-Orca is the Orca screen reader as packaged for Edukasaun OS and the
+Eduka-Desktop (LXQt). It speaks more slowly (rate 30 instead of 50) with a
+slightly lower voice (pitch 4.5 instead of 5.0), and shows everything it speaks
+as large captions at the bottom of the screen, to help users who are hard of
+hearing.
+.PP
+.B eduka-orca
+starts Orca with Qt accessibility enabled. All options are passed to
+.BR orca (1),
+for example
+.B \-\-replace
+or
+.BR \-\-setup .
+.PP
+.B eduka-orca-toggle
+turns the screen reader on or off, remembers the choice in the GSettings key
+.I org.gnome.desktop.a11y.applications screen-reader-enabled
+and shows a desktop notification.
+.PP
+.B eduka-orca-autostart
+is run by the LXQt session at login and starts Eduka-Orca only when that key is
+.IR true .
+The delay before starting can be changed with the environment variable
+.BR EDUKA_ORCA_START_DELAY
+(seconds, default 2).
+.SH FILES
+.TP
+.I /usr/share/doc/eduka-orca/README.Eduka.md
+Description of all Eduka changes and how to change the defaults system-wide.
+.TP
+.I /usr/share/eduka-orca/globalkeyshortcuts-eduka-orca.conf
+Super+Alt+S shortcut for lxqt-globalkeyshortcuts.
+.SH SEE ALSO
+.BR orca (1)
